rust/allocator: provide V2 ABI function symbols for Rust 1.92+

Rust 1.92 and later stdlib (liballoc) references V2-mangled allocator shim
symbols via R_X86_64_PLT32 relocations (function calls).  Chromium 138 only
defines the V1 symbols as static u8 data.  When a non-rustc linker drives the
final link (as Chromium does), the V2 symbols are never generated, so every
Rust allocation CALLs into a data byte and segfaults.

Add V2 function definitions with #[export_name] using the exact mangled names
liballoc expects:

  __rust_no_alloc_shim_is_unstable_v2  - no-op (return value ignored)
  __rust_alloc_error_handler_should_panic_v2 - returns 0 (abort on OOM)

V1 symbols are preserved for backward compatibility.

WARNING: the mangled names embed the __rustc crate disambiguator, which is
not stable across rustc releases.  These names are correct for rustc 1.98.1
(meta-lts-mixins scarthgap/rust, rust_1.98.1.bb).  They were previously
pinned to 1.92 and silently stopped matching, which surfaced as
"undefined symbol: __rustc::__rust_no_alloc_shim_is_unstable_v2" at link
time in chrome_crashpad_handler, mksnapshot and the yocto_native tools.
To re-derive after a rustc upgrade:

  nm -u <sysroot>/usr/lib/rustlib/<target>/lib/liballoc-*.rlib | grep _v2

and substitute the disambiguator that appears there.

Upstream-Status: Pending [ABI mismatch between Yocto Rust and Chromium 138]

diff --git a/build/rust/allocator/lib.rs b/build/rust/allocator/lib.rs
--- a/build/rust/allocator/lib.rs
+++ b/build/rust/allocator/lib.rs
@@ -90,12 +90,24 @@ mod both_allocators {
     #[linkage = "weak"]
     static __rust_no_alloc_shim_is_unstable: u8 = 0;
 
+    /// Rust 1.92+ V2 ABI: stdlib calls this as a function (PLT relocation),
+    /// not a data load.  Provide a no-op function with the exact mangled name.
+    #[export_name = "_RNvCshfJ12k0ydlO_7___rustc35___rust_no_alloc_shim_is_unstable_v2"]
+    #[linkage = "weak"]
+    extern "C" fn __rust_no_alloc_shim_is_unstable_v2() {}
+
     // Mangle the symbol name as rustc expects.
     #[rustc_std_internal_symbol]
     #[allow(non_upper_case_globals)]
     #[linkage = "weak"]
     static __rust_alloc_error_handler_should_panic: u8 = 0;
 
+    /// Rust 1.92+ V2 ABI: stdlib calls this as a function returning u8.
+    /// Return 0 = abort on alloc error (matches Chromium's static u8 = 0).
+    #[export_name = "_RNvCshfJ12k0ydlO_7___rustc42___rust_alloc_error_handler_should_panic_v2"]
+    #[linkage = "weak"]
+    extern "C" fn __rust_alloc_error_handler_should_panic_v2() -> u8 { 0 }
+
     // Mangle the symbol name as rustc expects.
     #[rustc_std_internal_symbol]
     #[allow(non_upper_case_globals)]
